---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Compact Objects Cheat Sheet | Free White Dwarfs, Neutron Stars, Black Holes"
  description="Complete compact objects cheat sheet with white dwarfs, neutron stars, and black holes. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Compact Objects<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>White dwarfs, neutron stars, and black holes. From stellar remnants to extreme physics.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>White Dwarfs</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Mass: < 1.4 M_sun (Chandrasekhar limit)
Radius: ~ Earth radius
Density: ~ 10⁹ kg/m³
Supported by: electron degeneracy pressure
Cools over time (no fusion)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Mass-Radius Relation</h3>
        <pre><code>R ∝ M^(-1/3) (more massive = smaller!)
Chandrasekhar limit: M_ch = 1.4 M_sun
Above limit: collapses to neutron star</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Neutron Stars</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Mass: 1.4-3 M_sun (TOV limit)
Radius: ~ 10 km
Density: ~ 10¹⁷ kg/m³
Supported by: neutron degeneracy pressure
Surface gravity: ~ 10¹² m/s²</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Special Types</h3>
        <pre><code>Pulsar: rotating, beamed radiation
Magnetar: B ~ 10⁸ T (strongest magnets)
X-ray binary: accreting neutron star
Millisecond pulsar: spun up by accretion</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Black Holes</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Schwarzschild Black Hole</h3>
        <pre><code>Event horizon: r_s = 2GM/c²
Singularity: r = 0 (infinite density)
No hair theorem: mass, charge, spin only
Hawking radiation: T = ℏc³/(8πGMk)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Types</h3>
        <pre><code>Stellar: 3-100 M_sun (stellar collapse)
Intermediate: 100-100,000 M_sun
Supermassive: 10⁶-10¹⁰ M_sun (galaxy centers)
Primordial: hypothetical (early universe)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Observational Signatures</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Detection Methods</h3>
        <pre><code>White dwarf: optical/UV emission
Neutron star: pulsar timing, X-ray
Black hole: X-ray binaries, gravitational lensing
Event horizon telescope: direct imaging</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
